\begin_layout Standard
Choosing the pure bare-metal path means implementing the complete,
 low-level serial frame protocol required to configure the external Infineon CYW43439 chip over a shared SPI-like layout.Because the CYW43439 relies on a dynamic host bus interface,
 setting a simple LED state requires communicating with its inner gSPI (generic SPI) module.
 On the Pico 2 W,
 this interface is wired directly to specific microchip pins rather than a standard peripheral controller,
 meaning we will use raw SVD registers to manually bit-bang the communication sequences.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Phase 1:
 Microcontroller Hardware Pin MappingTo control the external chip,
 configure the following four pins via your RP2350.GPIO SVD layout:GPIO 23 (WL_REG_ON):
 Power control/Hardware reset.
 Must be set as an Output.GPIO 25 (WL_CS):
 Chip Select.
 Must be set as an Output (Active Low).GPIO 29 (WL_CLK):
 SPI Clock line.
 Must be set as an Output.GPIO 24 (WL_DIO):
 Bi-directional data stream.
 Dynamically toggles between Output (sending frames) and Input (reading status).Phase 2:
 Implementation of the Pure Ada DriverTo keep your concurrent background task structure safe,
 encapsulate this entire bit-bang routine inside a Thread-Safe Protected Object.
 This configuration prevents other modules from interrupting a transmission mid-byte.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Phase 3:
 Update Your Library Task LooperUpdate your background task in your library architecture to replace the placeholder null;
 markers with explicit calls to your new,
 protected bare-metal driver:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Critical Troubleshooting NoteBecause we are directly manipulating data wires using high-speed software code execution,
 if your loops run too fast,
 the physical rising edges of your clock pin (GPIO 29) might not fully reach 3.3V before the data pin updates.
 If the LED doesn't start flashing right away,
 increase the loop bounds inside Bit_Bang_Write_32 (e.g.,
 change for J in 1 ..
 5 loop to 1 ..
 50) to stretch the signal timing window and help the Infineon chip interpret the data frame cleanly.
\end_layout

